note Exercism-style exercise "luhn": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/luhn
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note valid is true when s, after removing spaces, is at least two decimal digits (and nothing else)
note that pass the Luhn checksum.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/luhn
om2
fn valid s view uchar * to bool
n = ulong 0
t = ulong 0
for i ulong len s
c = get s sub sub len s 1 i
if eq c 32
continue
end
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret false
end
d = ulong sub c 48
if eq rem n 2 1
d = mul d 2
if gt d 9
d = sub d 9
end
end
t = add t d
n = add n 1
end
ret and gt n 1 eq rem t 10 0
end
